      "source": [
        "## Task 3: Model Architecture Design and Implementation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9b2a6a7c"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Model 1: 1D Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Architecture Description:**\n",
        "The CNN model for text classification will consist of the following layers:\n",
        "1.  **Embedding Layer:** Converts word indices into dense vectors of fixed size. This layer learns embeddings for each word, allowing words with similar meanings to have similar representations.\n",
        "2.  **Conv1D Layer:** Applies a 1D convolution operation to the embedded sequences. This layer extracts local features (like n-grams) from the text.\n",
        "3.  **GlobalMaxPool1D Layer:** Reduces the dimensionality of the feature maps by taking the maximum value across all time steps for each feature, capturing the most important features detected by the convolutional layer.\n",
        "4.  **Dense Layer:** A fully connected layer with a ReLU activation function for learning high-level representations.\n",
        "5.  **Dropout Layer:** A regularization technique to prevent overfitting by randomly setting a fraction of input units to 0 at each update during training.\n",
        "6.  **Output Dense Layer:** A single neuron with a sigmoid activation function for binary classification (positive/negative sentiment).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Architectural Choices Justification:**\n",
        "*   **Embedding Layer:** Essential for converting discrete word tokens into a continuous vector space, enabling the model to learn semantic relationships between words.\n",
        "*   **1D CNN:** Effective for identifying local patterns (like phrases or keyword combinations) that are indicative of sentiment, similar to how 2D CNNs detect features in images. It's computationally efficient.\n",
        "*   **GlobalMaxPool1D:** Aggregates the most salient features detected by the convolutional filters, providing a fixed-size output regardless of input length, suitable for feeding into dense layers.\n",
        "*   **Dense Layers with ReLU:** Standard choices for learning complex, non-linear relationships from the extracted features.\n",
        "*   **Dropout:** A crucial regularization technique to prevent the model from memorizing the training data, improving generalization to unseen data.\n",
        "*   **Sigmoid Activation (Output):** Appropriate for binary classification, outputting a probability score between 0 and 1.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Hyperparameters:**\n",
        "*   **Embedding Dimension:** 128 (a common size for word embeddings)\n",
        "*   **Filters (Conv1D):** 128\n",
        "*   **Kernel Size (Conv1D):** 5 (to detect 5-word sequences/n-grams)\n",
        "*   **Hidden Dense Units:** 128\n",
        "*   **Dropout Rate:** 0.5\n",
        "*   **Optimizer:** Adam\n",
        "*   **Loss Function:** Binary Cross-entropy\n",
        "*   **Batch Size:** 32 (a common batch size, balances memory usage and training speed)\n",
        "*   **Epochs:** Will be determined during training, usually 10-20 to start and monitor for convergence/overfitting.\n"
      ]
    },
