        "*   **LSTM Model:** Achieved a test accuracy of `0.8420` and a test loss of `0.7728`. The LSTM model showed a slower convergence compared to the CNN but also exhibited signs of overfitting, as its validation loss increased towards the end of training.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this specific task, the 1D CNN model demonstrated slightly better generalization performance on the IMDB sentiment classification dataset compared to the basic LSTM model. The ability of the CNN to effectively capture local features (n-grams) seems to have given it an edge for this particular dataset and `MAX_LEN`.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Future Work\n",
        "\n",
        "To further improve the models and explore more robust solutions, the following future steps could be considered:\n",
        "\n",
        "1.  **Hyperparameter Tuning:** Systematically tune hyperparameters (e.g., learning rate, dropout rate, number of filters/units, kernel size) for both models using techniques like GridSearchCV or RandomizedSearchCV.\n",
        "2.  **Advanced Embeddings:** Experiment with pre-trained word embeddings (e.g., Word2Vec, GloVe, FastText) or contextual embeddings (e.g., BERT, ELMo) which can capture more nuanced semantic relationships.\n",
        "3.  **Bi-directional LSTMs (BiLSTM):** Implement and evaluate a BiLSTM model, which processes sequences in both forward and backward directions, potentially capturing more context and improving performance over a unidirectional LSTM.\n",
        "4.  **Ensemble Methods:** Combine the predictions of the CNN and LSTM models to leverage their individual strengths.\n",
        "5.  **Attention Mechanisms:** Integrate attention layers into the models to allow them to focus on the most relevant parts of the input sequence for classification.\n",
        "6.  **Larger Datasets:** Evaluate the models on larger or more diverse sentiment analysis datasets to confirm their robustness.\n",
        "7.  **Early Stopping:** Implement early stopping callbacks during training to prevent overfitting by monitoring the validation loss and stopping training when it no longer improves.\n",
        "8.  **Regularization Techniques:** Explore additional regularization methods beyond dropout, such as L1/L2 regularization on weights.\n",
        "\n",
        "These steps would help to develop more powerful and generalizable models for text classification."
