        "### Model 2: Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) Network\n",
        "\n",
        "**Architecture Description:**\n",
        "The LSTM model for text classification will consist of the following layers:\n",
        "1.  **Embedding Layer:** Converts word indices into dense vectors of fixed size, similar to the CNN model.\n",
        "2.  **LSTM Layer:** This is the core recurrent layer. LSTMs are specifically designed to learn long-term dependencies in sequential data, making them highly effective for text. They have internal memory cells that can maintain information over long sequences.\n",
        "3.  **Dense Layer:** A fully connected layer with a ReLU activation function to learn high-level features from the LSTM output.\n",
        "4.  **Dropout Layer:** A regularization technique to prevent overfitting.\n",
        "5.  **Output Dense Layer:** A single neuron with a sigmoid activation function for binary classification.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Architectural Choices Justification:**\n",
        "*   **Embedding Layer:** As with the CNN, it's crucial for transforming discrete word tokens into a meaningful continuous vector space.\n",
        "*   **LSTM Layer:** Chosen for its proven ability to capture temporal relationships and long-range dependencies in sequential data like natural language. This allows the model to understand context across an entire review.\n",
        "*   **Dense Layers with ReLU:** Standard for processing the features extracted by the LSTM and learning non-linear mappings.\n",
        "*   **Dropout:** Essential for regularization to improve the model's generalization capabilities.\n",
        "*   **Sigmoid Activation (Output):** Appropriate for binary classification to output a probability.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Hyperparameters:**\n",
        "*   **Embedding Dimension:** 128 (consistent with CNN for fair comparison)\n",
        "*   **LSTM Units:** 128 (number of memory cells/output dimensionality)\n",
        "*   **Hidden Dense Units:** 128\n",
        "*   **Dropout Rate:** 0.5\n",
        "*   **Optimizer:** Adam\n",
        "*   **Loss Function:** Binary Cross-entropy\n",
        "*   **Batch Size:** 32 (consistent with CNN)\n",
        "*   **Epochs:** Will be determined during training."
      ]
    },
